{"name":"Bavarian","hex":"#4d5e42","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bavarian","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, from or relating to the state of Bavaria, Germany."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native or inhabitant of the state of Bavaria, Germany.","Alternative form of bavarian (“fruit-based dessert”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bavarian"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baiuvarii","blocks":[{"text":"The Baiuvarii, Baiovari or early Bavarians were a Germanic people who are first mentioned in contemporary records starting in the 6th century, soon after the end of the Western Roman Empire. They originally lived in what had been the Roman province Raetia, south of the Danube, in what is now southern Bavaria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Roman_Bavaria.png/330px-Roman_Bavaria.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baiuvarii","wikidata":"Q156740"},{"title":"Bavarians","blocks":[{"text":"Bavarians are an ethnographic group of Germans native to Bavaria, a state in Germany. The group's dialect or language is known as Bavarian, native to Altbayern, roughly the territory of the historic Electorate of Bavaria in the 17th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Flag_of_Bavaria_%28lozengy%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Bavaria_%28lozengy%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bavarians","wikidata":"Q13048507"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Bairisches_Mundartgebiet.PNG/500px-Bairisches_Mundartgebiet.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Bairisches_Mundartgebiet.PNG/500px-Bairisches_Mundartgebiet.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont